<title>UNITED NATIONS: IAEA director Blix to leave post in a year.</title>
<headline>IAEA director Blix to leave post in a year.</headline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hans Blix, director-general of the International Atomic Energy Agency, said on Thursday he would leave his post in a year and retire to Sweden.</p>
<p>Blix, a former Swedish foreign minister, has headed the Vienna-based U.N. nuclear watchdog agency since 1981. He said he would not seek another extension when his current term expires at the end of 1997.</p>
<p>Asked what he would do then, he told reporters: &quot;Go home, to Sweden.&quot;</p>
<p>The IAEA tries to prevent the diversion of nuclear technology to military uses and to promote peaceful uses of nuclear energy.</p>
</text>
